 "schema": "pcc.claim/v1",
 "scope": "Lean 4.35.0 / CryptoLean 01750b40 / Mathlib cfc55fc5; lattice model of O_f as Submodule \u2124 (\u2124\u00d7\u2124); TransferBound/DeepGap abstract monoid solvers; End(E)\u2243O_f and Robert Remark 4.5 poly(log \u2113) volcano navigation remain unformalized bridges (documented, not axiomatized).",
 "statement": "Ordinary conductor prime gaps are lattice-orthogonal to smooth/small-degree isogeny walks: a padicValNat gap forces an \u2113-power into step degrees and a step with \u2113|d and \u2113\u2264d. From a Frobenius discriminant with D\u2080\u2264\u22123 one has 3 f\u2080\u00b2 \u2264 4 q, and TransferBound chains separate always-correct solvers by exactly twice the isogeny-cost sum. Above the floor, scalar Frobenius acts with (\u2124/\u2113)\u02e3-centralizer transitivity on the \u2113+1 projective lines, so adaptive membership decision lists need \u2265\u2113 queries to cover all lines; (ZMod \u2113)\u02e3 is cyclic of order \u2113\u22121. Floor endomorphisms in \u2113\u00b7O have quadraticNorm divisible by \u2113\u00b2 (blocking odd-\u2113 Kani 2-power norms), and Hasse-interval traces satisfying a quadratic congruence mod \u2113 are O(B/\u2113)-thin. Kernel Lucas certificates pin the ECC2K-130-scale primes 263 and 146505763881528721 and the deep-volcano prime 631409; a conductor-1 crater walk ending at conductor 1 has no vertical valuation gap."
}
